{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q104967085","formula":"C₂₀H₂₀O₇","hill":"C20H20O7","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":20.0,"O":7.0},"names":{"en":"Nephroarctin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Nephroarctin is a naturally occurring depside compound found in certain foliose lichens, most notably Nephroma arcticum from which it was first isolated in 1969. Along with its related compound phenarctin, it is one of two structurally unusual compounds produced by N. arcticum, both characterised by an uncommonly high number of single-carbon attachments to their core structure. This colourless crystalline substance, with the molecular formula C20H20O7, consists of two benzene rings connected by an ester linkage and plays a role in the lichen's defensive mechanisms."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":597224,"mass":372.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=C(C(=C1C)OC(=O)C2=C(C(=C(C(=C2C)C=O)O)C=O)O)C)OC","inchikey":"COJRBNIKTUZKMH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"(3-methoxy-2,5,6-trimethylphenyl) 3,5-diformyl-2,4-dihydroxy-6-methylbenzoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"597224","atoms":47,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.829,"y":-0.202,"z":0.602,"el":"O"},{"x":5.086,"y":1.972,"z":0.343,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.439,"y":-2.38,"z":-0.538,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.402,"y":0.149,"z":0.327,"el":"O"},{"x":0.653,"y":-0.002,"z":-1.715,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.143,"y":2.769,"z":-0.015,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.227,"y":-2.494,"z":0.596,"el":"O"},{"x":2.808,"y":-1.499,"z":0.271,"el":"C"},{"x":2.216,"y":-0.266,"z":0.447,"el":"C"},{"x":2.943,"y":0.905,"z":0.476,"el":"C"},{"x":4.193,"y":-1.563,"z":0.116,"el":"C"},{"x":4.328,"y":0.841,"z":0.321,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.306,"y":-0.001,"z":-0.354,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.933,"y":1.228,"z":-0.146,"el":"C"},{"x":4.953,"y":-0.393,"z":0.141,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.308,"y":1.278,"z":0.083,"el":"C"},{"